[ledge] The undersides of the 1 mm exterior retaining tabs' 1.25 mm lateral overhangs. The cover prints on its interior flange, so these face the bed, 4.9 mm up. They are the tabs' supported faces, accessible before installation, with the 0.25 mm supported-face allowance in their 0.50 mm wall clearance (copper-plugs/README.md).
alternatives: Tabs flush with the web lose the inward stop that holds the cover before the pour. A 45° underside thickens the tab toward the wall and closes its clearance.
